\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Whose eyes:
\f1\b0 \'a0Jamison Hardy's, start to finish, with the narrator taking the last word. Two centuries before Part 1. He comes off the referenced-only list for this chapter and goes straight back onto it.\

\f0\b The register:
\f1\b0 \'a0office admin. Not a thriller, not a horror. Hardy is courteous, tidy, faintly sad and entirely convinced he is doing something noble, and he is never once shown enjoying any of it. Nobody raises their voice in the whole chapter. The cruelty is in the paperwork.\

\f0\b What changes:
\f1\b0 \'a0it opens with a cure for every human disease in existence and Hardy the only man alive who has been told. It closes with the cure under fifty metres of rock along with the people who made it, and Hardy certain he is a hero \'97 and right that nobody will ever know.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

