\f0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No villain speech.
\f1\b0 \'a0Hardy never explains the economics of illness to anybody. Dunhilton recites that finding as his own common sense two centuries later, having never heard of the room it came out of, and the echo is the payment.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Nobody dies on the page.
\f1\b0 \'a0No glass dome, no cook-up, no murdered security manager \'97 first-draft scaffolding, and all of it weaker than the invoice.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Nobody pleads, struggles, or bangs on a door.
\f1\b0 \'a0The last thing in the room is a man being embarrassed about his lift home.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Hardy is never cruel and never doubts.
\f1\b0 \'a0No flicker of conscience he acts on, no hesitation the reader can bank. Courtesy the whole way through.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No character in the rest of the book ever learns any of this.
\f1\b0 \'a0Gerry's\'a0
\f4\i "Apparently not"
\f1\i0 \'a0stays a shrug forever. Sarah knows what happened to her mother and nothing whatever about that conference room.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No date, no caption.
\f1\b0 \'a0No year on the page and no\'a0
\f4\i two hundred years later
\f1\i0 \'a0\'97 the narrator's closing sentence carries the time by itself.\
